      "text": "To find the value of \\( z \\), we need to use the formula for the projection of a vector \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) onto a vector \\(\\mathbf{b}\\). The projection of \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) onto \\(\\mathbf{b}\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\n\nGiven vectors are:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate the dot product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 0 \\cdot (-3) + 3 \\cdot 5 + z \\cdot (-1) = 0 + 15 - z = 15 - z\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the dot product \\(\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = (-3)^2 + 5^2 + (-1)^2 = 9 + 25 + 1 = 35\n\\]\n\nNow, we use the projection formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nWe are given that the projection is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThus, we equate the two expressions for the projection:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nSince the vectors are equal, their scalar coefficients must be equal. Therefore, we set up the equation:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} = \\frac{12}{35}\n\\]\n\nBy equating the numerators, we get:\n\n\\[\n15 - z = 12\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( z \\):\n\n\\[\n15 - 12 = z \\implies z = 3\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( z \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
